    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607">

                <pb facs="0867" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1320a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Feely</hi>)<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d607-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-05T18:00:00-04:00">August 5, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Department’s telegram No. 40 dated July 30. Neutral governments have approved
                    text of note to Bolivian Government. You will therefore deliver it on behalf of
                    the United States on August 6.</p>
                <p>In the event that Colombia and Cuba have no representatives in La Paz you will
                    present the note on behalf of each of these governments. If there are such
                    representatives and they have not received the text of the note you will deliver
                    to them this text, in order that they may present the note in person.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d607-f1" n="81" type="source" xml:id="d607-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Chargé in
                    Paraguay as telegram No. 30, referring to Department’s telegram No. 29, July 30,
                    7 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
